# The watchdog's times (src/product/watchdog.ts, mica-core watchdog-20261115): the signed boot policy's
# board.watchdog handoverS (the timeout the runkit asks the driver for at the handover) and confirmS (the uptime a
# trial boot has to be confirmed in before it is failed and the device reboots). Absent, core's defaults: 120 s and
# 900 s. Kept out of board.env on purpose: board.env is an input of the board package and component.
# handoverS stays at core's default on every board: the feeder takes the device within seconds of the handover.
# confirmS: PROVISIONAL (UBI: the attach and the first mount, the scan after a power cut) until a bench measures
# a first boot and a trial boot.
BOARD_WATCHDOG_CONFIRM_S=1800
